            <ArticleTitle>Withdrawal symptoms from transdermal fentanyl (TDF) after an allogeneic peripheral blood stem cell transplant (PBSCT).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>164-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 47-year-old woman who underwent allogenic peripheral blood stem cell transplant developed withdrawal symptoms soon after Fentanyl 25 mcg/h patch was stopped, which has not been reported at this dose. Possible causes, such as the inhibition of CYP3A4 induced by cyclosporine causing elevations of serum fentanyl, are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
